Jahshaka patch 0044 — the irradiance field can be MOVED, and can be told its
VctLighting re-created the textures it reads.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this (reset the ogre-next submodule first if it already carries an
earlier revision of any patch: `git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- .
&& git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next clean -fd`).

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A REACH-IN (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325). Photon's
E1 stage puts the irradiance field on the innermost cascade of a camera-centred
chain, so the field's volume has to follow that cascade as it scrolls. Upstream
has no way to say so: `initialize()` is the only placement API and it calls
`createTextures()`, which destroys and re-creates both atlases (and the
compositor workspace, the directions buffer and the integration taps) — a field
re-initialized on every step is born black on every step. Everything else in the
class already reads the placement LIVE (`fillConstBufferData` rebuilds the pixel
transform per pass, `IrradianceFieldRaster::renderProbes` derives each probe
camera from it), so the missing piece is a placement setter, not a rebuild. The
members it would need — `mFieldOrigin`, `mFieldSize`,
`setIrradianceFieldGenParams()` — are `protected`, i.e. exactly the reach-in the
rule forbids; the hook is added where it belongs instead.

  1. `setFieldVolume( origin, size )` — moves/resizes the volume in place,
     applying the same one-probe-block enlargement `initialize()` applies, and
     re-derives the generation params (which carry the probe-to-voxel transform,
     so they must be re-derived whenever the field OR the voxel volume moved).
     The probe counts are settings and are untouched, so the atlases stay valid
     and keep the irradiance integrated at the previous placement; whether to
     `reset()` and re-converge progressively over it or to converge the whole
     field in one `update()` is the caller's policy decision.

  2. `setVctLighting( lighting )` — A DEFECT IN THE PIN, not only a missing hook.
     `IrradianceField::createTextures()` binds `VctLighting::getLightVoxelTextures()`
     into the generation job ONCE, by pointer, and nothing ever re-binds them.
     But a `VctLighting` re-creates those textures whenever its voxelizer's
     textures change: `checkTextures()` does it on any LostResidency/Deleted
     notification (a device loss, a texture pool shuffle), and `setVoxelizer()`
     (patch 0037) does it on purpose. After either, a field bound to that
     lighting integrates from destroyed textures — freed GPU memory, or whatever
     the allocator has since handed those addresses to, silently. There is no
     notification from VctLighting to its readers at this pin, so the answer is
     a hook the reader can be given: passing the SAME lighting is meaningful and
     re-binds. It also re-asserts `vct_anisotropic` and the tex-unit count, which
     may differ between two lightings, and re-derives the generation params.

Both are no-ops on a raster-sourced field (it has no VctLighting and no
generation-job bindings; its probe cameras read the volume live).

Verified: `git apply --check` against the pristine pin and `git apply --reverse
--check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane worktree; the
`--engine-selftest` hash is unchanged (`b55e2d5d…`) — no existing call site
reaches either function.

